# Contact form delivery. Everything here is optional.
#
# Leave this file alone and the form still works: it opens the visitor's own
# mail app with the whole ticket written out, and the ticket screen tells them
# to press send. No account, no service, no cost. The catch is that it needs a
# mail app configured, so a visitor on webmail-only sees nothing happen.
#
# Set a relay and the message is sent for you instead, with the visitor never
# leaving the page. Pick whichever of these you can actually get into, then
# fill that block in in .env or .env.local — both are gitignored, and this
# file is the only one of the family that gets committed.
#
# Vite reads these once, at startup. Restart `npm run dev` after a change, and
# set the same variable in your host's project settings for a deployed build:
# .env never leaves your machine.
#
# None of these values are secrets. A form key is a delivery address: it can
# only post a message to the one mailbox it belongs to, and it is visible in
# the built bundle whatever you do. Every provider lets you lock it to your
# domain once the site is live.

# --- Web3Forms --------------------------------------------------------------
# Free plan: 250 messages a month. You give them the inbox you want messages
# delivered to and the key is emailed straight back. The ~$13/mo Pro plan buys
# webhooks, file uploads and a submissions API, none of which this form uses.
# Set the key on its own and the endpoint is assumed.
VITE_W3F_KEY=

# --- Formspree --------------------------------------------------------------
# Free plan: 50 messages a month. Create a form, copy its endpoint.
# VITE_FORM_ENDPOINT=https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxxxx

# --- FormSubmit -------------------------------------------------------------
# Free, no account at all: the endpoint is your email address. First submission
# sends you a confirmation link. Swap the address for the hashed alias it gives
# you afterwards, or the address sits in the bundle for scrapers to find.
# VITE_FORM_ENDPOINT=https://formsubmit.co/ajax/your-hashed-alias

# --- Anything else ----------------------------------------------------------
# Any endpoint that accepts a JSON POST works. VITE_FORM_KEY is sent as
# `access_key` if the service wants one.
# VITE_FORM_ENDPOINT=
# VITE_FORM_KEY=
